13. Add save and load functionality:
* In the game instance blueprint, create variables to store the player's progress, such as current level, player health, inventory, etc.
* In the game instance blueprint, create functions to save the game to a file and load the game from a file.
* In the player character blueprint, call the save and load functions at appropriate times (e.g. when the player presses the save button, when the game starts, etc.).

Example game instance blueprint code:
```scss
UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere, BlueprintReadWrite, Category = "Save")
FString SaveFileName = "SaveGame";

void SaveGame()
{
    USaveGame* SaveGameInstance = USaveGame::CreateSaveGameInstance();
    SaveGameInstance->CurrentLevel = CurrentLevel;
    SaveGameInstance->PlayerHealth = PlayerHealth;
    SaveGameInstance->Inventory = Inventory;
    UGameplayStatics::SaveGameToSlot(SaveGameInstance, SaveFileName, 0);
}

void LoadGame()
{
    USaveGame* SaveGameInstance = UGameplayStatics::LoadGameFromSlot(SaveFileName, 0);
    if (SaveGameInstance)
    {
        CurrentLevel = SaveGameInstance->CurrentLevel;
        PlayerHealth = SaveGameInstance->PlayerHealth;
        Inventory = SaveGameInstance->Inventory;
    }
}
```
